= Data leakage — Simple =

'''Data leakage''' happens when a machine-learning system accidentally gets information it should not have during training or evaluation.

For example:

* a feature includes information created after the answer is already known;
* test examples are mixed into training data;
* preprocessing is calculated using the whole dataset before the split;
* the same person appears in both training and test sets in a way that reveals the answer.

Leakage can make a model look much better than it really is.

This is different from security data leaks or stolen files.

